Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.4.0
================================================================================
+ Configurable per-connection object ACL with warning for non-public ACLs requiring a CDN URL [#24]
+ Machine-translated language packs for Greek, French, German, Spanish, Italian, and Portuguese [#27]
~ Raised minimum requirements to PHP 8.1 and Joomla 5.4; dropped support for PHP 7.4–8.0 and Joomla 4.x; capped support at PHP 8.6 and Joomla 6.2
# [HIGH] With v4 signatures and path-style access, public URLs put the bucket in the host name, so they did not load
# [MEDIUM] Folders created outside Joomla (e.g. with the AWS CLI or CyberDuck) could not be deleted
# [MEDIUM] Searching a folder with more than 1,000 files never finished, tying up the server and repeating S3 requests
# [MEDIUM] TLS host name verification was off for default (dual-stack) and China Amazon S3 connections
# [MEDIUM] S3 uploads ignored the Media Manager's upload restrictions (forbidden extensions, MIME and XSS checks)
# [MEDIUM] File and folder names could contain quotes and HTML, enabling stored XSS when inserted with some editors
# [MEDIUM] Custom region lookup typo (connection['$region'] → connection['custom_region']) broke the "Custom" region option
# [LOW] The "Requests caching time" option's description was shown wrapped in curly quotes
# [LOW] The package shipped the S3 library's test harness and other development files
# [LOW] Updating left behind files that older versions shipped (the old bundled S3 library and form rules)
# [LOW] A failed thumbnail raised a PHP warning with the site's path, and thumbnail cache folders had no index.html
# [LOW] Storage errors showed bucket names and raw S3 error details to every Media Manager user
# [LOW] Copying or moving a file whose name has %, + or ? could copy a different object, or fail
# [LOW] Cached listings showed file dates in the timezone and language of whoever loaded them first
# [LOW] Paths containing '..' reached S3 instead of being refused, unlike Joomla's own Media Manager
# [LOW] Uppercase file extensions were not lowercased on upload, unlike Joomla's own Media Manager
# [LOW] Dead code in custom endpoint protocol detection (':\' instead of '://'); defaulted to useSSL=true so no working configuration was affected
# [LOW] Escape the Content-Disposition filename in createFile to neutralise quote / backslash / CR / LF
# [LOW] New PathNormaliser strips NUL / CR / LF / '#' / '?' from the configured directory and applies Unicode NFC (ext-intl optional)

Amazon S3 Filesystem for Joomla 1.3.1
================================================================================
# [HIGH] Custom S3-compatible CDN provider ignores the Custom Endpoint URL [#22]

